guys came up with the big sign and they're like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:00.960 --> 01:33:03.680
"What the hell's going on?" They get escorted&nbsp;
out and then Bill Burr's like, "What the hell's&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:03.680 --> 01:33:08.600
going — the Napster sign? What do these guys do?"
It worked like a charm. So this thing was going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:08.600 --> 01:33:15.760
go, and it was like within a week of going, and&nbsp;
I'm 22 years old and this thing would've been&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:15.760 --> 01:33:20.800
something real. This overshot the GQ magazine&nbsp;
cover that I had dreamed of or whatever. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:20.800 --> 01:33:26.040
anyway, so the client has to go to the Napster&nbsp;
board to give them a progress update. And the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:26.040 --> 01:33:31.120
Napster client is under no responsibility to share&nbsp;
launch ideas or activations. This fell under. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:31.120 --> 01:33:34.480
the client goes to the board and says, "Okay,&nbsp;
here's our strategy and we're going to go to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:34.480 --> 01:33:38.920
