and do a show. I don't know if it ages well.&nbsp;
I think because the humor can be — so please&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:24.880 --> 01:38:29.538
don't judge me if the subject matter is not PC.
Tim Ferriss: You can judge me. It's pretty funny.&nbsp;

01:38:29.538 --> 01:38:32.240
Chris Beresford-Hill: Judge Tim. So that one&nbsp;
goes to Tim because he likes that show too.&nbsp;

01:38:32.240 --> 01:38:38.720
Tim Ferriss: I will say that it's an amazing&nbsp;
doc/mini-doc. There are a couple of points&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:38.720 --> 01:38:42.698
where it drags a little bit, but there are&nbsp;
so many payoffs. There's so many payoffs.&nbsp;

01:38:42.698 --> 01:38:46.280
Chris Beresford-Hill: No, but even&nbsp;
just the thing of when — which one&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:46.280 --> 01:38:49.098
is the blonde one? Is that Trey?
Tim Ferriss: I can't remember.&nbsp;

01:38:49.098 --> 01:38:52.640
Chris Beresford-Hill: He's like the writer, writer&nbsp;
out of the two of them. And once they've got the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:52.640 --> 01:38:58.000
story down and he has to write the script, he has&nbsp;
his assistant go get him an extra value meal from&nbsp;&nbsp;

